.SH NAME
daharness\-safety \(em daharness safety model: scope gate, approvals,
budgets, retention
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SS Scope gate (operator\-armed only)
Traffic\-sending tools resolve every target through an operator\-armed
scope state.
Arming happens ONLY at the operator REPL (\f[CR]scope on <handle>\f[R])
and is deliberately NOT exposed as an LLM\-callable tool, so no model lane
can toggle it.
State persists across processes (the REPL can re\-arm a running Brain).
Blocked targets raise a scope error instead of transmitting.
.SS Human\-in\-the\-loop approval
There is no in\-process approval loop: the secretary chat lane
(pydantic\-ai) was removed 2026\-10\-20.
Tool calls through the API gateway or MCP execute under their own gates
\(em the operator\-armed scope gate, the per\-turn budget and the
ROUTER_MAX_DISTANCE abstention.
An integrating harness that wants sign\-off adds its own approval in
front of the gateway.
.SS Per\-turn tool budget
Gateway lanes (REST/MCP/Open WebUI) enforce a hard cap on tool
executions per turn; the final allowed call is wrapped with a directive
to report findings and end the turn; further calls are refused with
structured guidance (not a transient error).
Terminal\-lane tools (memory, findings, unknowns) stay callable past the
cap so the model can comply.
.SS Gateway bind + auth posture
The REST/MCP gateway binds GATEWAY_HOST:GATEWAY_PORT \(em loopback
(127.0.0.1:5000) in this profile.
GATEWAY_API_KEY arms key auth (X\-API\-Key or Bearer) over the whole
REST + /mcp surface; the packaged profile generates a random key at
install (postinst), so a stock deb never boots an off\-host
tool\-execution gateway unauthenticated.
.PP
With or without a key, /docs, /redoc, /openapi.json and /health stay
unauthenticated by design (spec + liveness reachability) \(em remember
this when widening the bind: anything on 0.0.0.0 advertises the full API
surface shape via openapi.json.
Unauthenticated AND non\-loopback together logs a boot\-time error
rather than serving silently.
.SS Local\-only LLM policy
The models driving the lanes (Open WebUI conversation model, embedding
model) run on a locally hosted endpoint (Ollama, loopback/LAN) \(em never
a cloud LLM API.
Tool outputs from live targets (credentials, tokens, internal IPs) must
not egress to third parties.
.SS Engagement cobweb
An engagement\(aqs rows (journal, evidence, findings, unknowns) unify
under one slug, so a purge erases one engagement in a single transaction
while the journal audit trail stays append\-only until the operator
closes it.
Arming is REPL\-only.
.SS Engagement\-Postgres lane (optional)
Off by default: no Postgres server ships; the journal runs on the SQLite
stores.
\f[CR]sudo daharness\-pg init\f[R] provisions a \f[B]dedicated\f[R]
Postgres cluster (\f[CR]daharness\f[R], port 5433) whose fate msfdb can
never touch (msf\(aqs own \f[CR]main\f[R] cluster keeps 5432), creates
one no\-superuser LOGIN role per lane
(harness_operator/brain_lane/gateway_lane/repl_lane), and mints random
per\-role passwords into \f[CR]/etc/daharness/pg.env\f[R] (0640
root:daharness).
Lanes hold INSERT/SELECT (+ evidence UPDATE); \f[B]no lane ever holds
DELETE\f[R] \(em purge runs as a SECURITY DEFINER owner function the
operator alone calls.
The server listens on loopback only with password auth (scram\-sha\-256
on current Kali\(aqs PG 18); the operator REPL reaches it via group
membership.
Postgres absent or the cluster down = honest degrade back to SQLite
stores, logged once, never a crash.
.SS Credential\-reuse sweep
Every recovered credential gets ONE validation attempt against each
other reachable service before deeper work resumes \(em logged as
findings, auditable in the evidence store.
